Z||000000||Galen||07-09-2001||09:47 AM||||As the subject said..<P>Blue Dingy Thing is not very PC.. and this is why..<P>"Blue Dingy Thing".. lets break it down. <P>Blue: Perhaps this should be Plutonian, or perhaps just blue.<P>Dingy: The blonde crowd may dislike this term. Therefore we must change this to something a little less offensive, Like perhaps .. "Noise producer". In my opinion it does not offend me, and it should not offend others.<P>Thing: This word makes one assume that this warning device is not needed., which I am sure it would find offensive and would be very upset and start chiming whenever the devil it felt like it. And that, is bad. So, we shall replace it with.. "box made of plastic that fits under the dash to warn you".<P>Now lets see.. now we have "Blue Noise Producer box made of plastic that fits under the dash to warn you", now doesn't that sound a little less offensive?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/redcreature.gif">   <BR><FONT SIZE="1">To whom it may concern, The preceeding message was the opinion of this person and not of this forum. If you do not like it. Oh well</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000001||84Bill||07-09-2001||10:07 AM||||I think one needs to jump in a <B>blue dingy</B> and row across the atlantic to a remote island some where and do there own <B>thingy</B> and not bother the rest of us with trivial stuff.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||12
Z||000002||Steve Normington||07-09-2001||11:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>Now lets see.. now we have "Blue Noise Producer box made of plastic that fits under the dash to warn you", now doesn't that sound a little less offensive?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You have at least six highly offensive sections:<BR>1) "Blue" - references to color are NEVER acceptable.<BR>2) "Noise" - who are you to determine which sounds are noise and which are music?<BR>3) "box" - implies shape-ism.<BR>4) "plastic" - never PC in any form.<BR>5) "under" - implies that this item is somehow inferior to the dash.<BR>6) "to warn you" - you are dictating the function of this item, this item has the freedom to do and be anything it wants to be.<P>So, the truly PC term would be, "Producer that fits the dash." Just like any truly PC name, this one means nothing. ||||reg||1
